.TH UOO-BOOT-INSPECT 1 "October 2026" "Uoo Boot Manager" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
uoo-boot-inspect \- inspect the installed Uoo helper and available boot data
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B uoo-boot-inspect
.RB [ --probe ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Print a JSON response with the installed version and helper availability.
Without an option, also include the boot configuration visible to the user.
This command does not apply changes or request administrator authentication.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --probe
Report version and installed-helper availability without reading boot settings.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates a successful response. A nonzero status indicates an error;
the JSON response includes its description.
.SH AUTHOR
Hayk Jomardyan.
